    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal lineup for the Austin Waves is anchored by **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56), both of whom benefit from favorable matchups against high-xERA starters. **Jackson Merrill** is a particularly high-upside play today; facing Pfaadt, his score is bolstered by a slow opposing delivery that increases his stolen base expectancy, a vital factor for our scarcity-driven strategy. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a strong platoon advantage against McGreevy, cementing his position in the #3 hole and providing the highest floor of our infield contingent. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (74.07) remains a core start despite the slight drag from dynamic platoon adjustments, as he draws a highly favorable matchup against Javier\u2019s 5.27 xERA.\n\nOn the periphery, **Kyle Tucker** (65.22) and **Andy Pages** (61.68) provide solid production against Boyd, though **Andy Pages** faces a cautionary note regarding the opposing pitcher\u2019s 62% success rate in controlling the running game, which slightly depresses his score. **Cole Carrigg** (57.84) and **Nasim Nunez** (55.15) occupy the bottom of our start-worthy threshold. While **Cole Carrigg** benefits from a massive 14% park adjustment, his score is capped by a challenging matchup against Seymour. **Nasim Nunez** represents our most marginal start; while he is currently active, we are closely monitoring the game against Nola, whose 4.00 xERA remains the most formidable obstacle our hitters will face this afternoon.\n\nLooking at the bench, we are navigating a difficult slate where **Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jacob Wilson** are unavailable due to scheduling, while **Jordan Westburg** remains on the IL. Consequently, there was no true \"tough cut\" today as our active roster depth is severely thinned by these absences. We are essentially running out our best available options by default. We will keep a close eye on the weather and late-scratch potential for **Nasim Nunez** and **Cole Carrigg**; if conditions deteriorate or lineups shift, we lack the depth to pivot significantly, meaning our success today rests on the core performance of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Jackson Merrill** to drive the stat sheet in the absence of our heavy hitters like **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, and **Coby Mayo**.",
